From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: training items
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

Training's item (tweak patch 0038) was only ever one of a power-up, while
the game also awards three or five (AwardPowerup: every shell but the red one
and the banana and the Bob-omb come in fives too, the red shell in threes)
and the captains' own power-ups. The launcher now chooses those too.

cGame::ResetPowerups gives the team that trains as many as the launcher
says. Item 9, which in ePowerUpType is Mario's, stands for the power-up of
whichever captain trains (CharacterInfo::mCaptainPowerup); as AwardPowerup,
it gives none to a shattered captain (Crystal Canyon's flares).

A single shell, banana or Bob-omb is thrown medium or giant at random
(BuildPowerupThrowParameters, Shell, Banana and Bobomb Medium Chance); a
giant one of the launcher's is always giant, as the giant cheat throws a
single one, for the team that trains only.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
index a4cccff..4879d9d 100644
--- a/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_tweaks.h
@@ -228,6 +228,11 @@ int mscharged_tweak_training_away_skill(void);
 // Whether the pad that starts the match plays the away team (the home one
 // otherwise).
 bool mscharged_tweak_training_play_away(void);
+// And how many of its item the team that trains gets (1, 3 or 5), and whether
+// a single one is always thrown giant; item 9 stands for the power-up of the
+// captain that trains.
+int mscharged_tweak_training_item_count(void);
+bool mscharged_tweak_training_item_giant(void);
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
diff --git a/src/Game/AI/Powerups.cpp b/src/Game/AI/Powerups.cpp
index 59092c6..6676008 100644
